[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. It is not one bug. The desk
merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every one of
these reports has a subject like "wrong day" or "dates mixed up", whatever broke the date. Read by
tenant, channel and body, the reports split into three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other two keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. Day and month swap: "booked for 2 March, the invite says 3 February". This is the bug
#4471 names, and the fix it has queued.

**`hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`; booking-v2 prints `DD/MM/YYYY`. A day-first tenant's people follow the hint, and
the form reads what they typed the tenant's way. The symptom is the same swap, but it comes from
the form, so the parser fix does not touch it. It only reaches reports sent through the form of a
booking-v3 tenant.

**`one-day-move`: the date moves by a day.** No swap: "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday",
"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday, client in Toronto got Monday". That is a time-zone shift. The desk
already listed these reports apart in its notes, but counted them under `parser`.

## How to tell them apart

- Do not trust the intake tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser; the cause depends on
  the tenant's locale, its booking form and the channel (`causes.ts`). The two disagree often.
- A swap through a booking-v3 form is `hint`. Any other swap is `parser`.
- A date one day off is `one-day-move`, whatever the subject says.
- One id is one report: the ticket export repeats some reports, and they count once.

## What changes for the desk

- Merge new reports into the ticket for their problem, not into the ticket with the same subject.
- Keep #4471 for the parser. Close it only when the parser fix ships and the other two tickets
  are open on their own.

